1
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,490
Let us prepare for Prince Zardos' arrival.

2
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:45,190
My dear General, what do you have to say
to me, Draco?

3
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:49,290
Our army is ready to fight.

4
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:52,010
Zandra.

5
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:58,010
I do not expect anything from us,
especially from the Terra Earth army.

6
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:02,830
Zul, everything is ready, Prince Zardos.

7
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,770
We are just waiting for your order.

8
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:15,920
My order is to surrender the planet Terra
Earth.

9
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:08,680
They're here.

10
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:15,850
Captain, Mr. O'Planet, are you alert?

11
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,490
The Bosanians have arrived.

12
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:18,570
Aye, sir.

13
00:03:46,170 --> 00:03:48,710
Sir, all stations report ready.

14
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:55,320
Attention, all nations of the Earth
Defense Forces.

15
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:59,120
This is your Supreme Commander,
General Robinson, speaking.

16
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:03,600
We have confirmed that a large alien force
has entered the Earth's atmosphere.

17
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:08,830
All international sectors must immediately
implement all defense protocols.

18
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:11,580
May God save us all.

19
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,160
The whole world is doing everything to
defend our planet.

20
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,580
But we are no match to these invaders,
sir.

21
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:53,980
Also, we are receiving a report that
aliens are spreading all around the globe.

22
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:57,600
Sir, there's fear and chaos everywhere.

23
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:02,300
I'm afraid that these aliens might succeed
in invading us if we don't stop them.

24
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:11,780
We have no hope if it's not our last line
of defense, the Voltis V.

25
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:21,180
Jamie Robinson, return to base.

26
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:22,580
Roger that.

27
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:45,990
Little John Armstrong, return to base.

28
00:07:46,610 --> 00:07:47,030
Yes, sir.

29
00:07:54,730 --> 00:07:57,170
Big Bird Armstrong, return to base.

30
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,000
Mark Gordon, return to base.

31
00:08:26,970 --> 00:08:28,950
Steve Armstrong, return to base.

32
00:08:29,230 --> 00:08:29,730
On the way.

33
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:49,370
Red alert.

34
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:50,670
Red alert.

35
00:08:51,370 --> 00:08:52,570
All crew to battle station.

36
00:08:52,570 --> 00:08:55,530
Ma, what's going on?

37
00:08:55,610 --> 00:08:57,010
Why do you know everything about the camp?

38
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,090
Maybe it's on a need-to-know basis.

39
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:04,050
At least I don't have a mother who works
here.

40
00:09:04,970 --> 00:09:05,750
But them?

41
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:08,730
They're your family.

42
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:12,730
The least you could do is tell them what
all this training is for.

43
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:20,400
I guess there's no more reason for me to
keep the truth from all of you.

44
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:24,610
Observe.

45
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:31,050
The world is under attack by an alien
menace.

46
00:09:47,350 --> 00:09:49,070
And you...

47
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:51,590
will save the world.

48
00:09:52,710 --> 00:09:53,510
Our world.

49
00:09:59,090 --> 00:09:59,950
Aliens?

50
00:10:00,790 --> 00:10:01,850
Did I hear that right?

51
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:03,230
Aliens?

52
00:10:03,730 --> 00:10:06,210
What you told us before is true,
Dr. Smith.

53
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:08,770
I thought it was a joke.

54
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:14,770
We'll save the world from these aliens.

55
00:10:15,130 --> 00:10:18,210
So you're saying we're in the middle of an
interplanetary war?

56
00:10:21,810 --> 00:10:23,450
Ma, this is the truth.

57
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:30,050
Yes, Steve.

58
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:32,990
This is the reason why you're mothers.

59
00:10:34,090 --> 00:10:35,810
That's why we made a Voltess robot.

60
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:40,850
Because we've known for a long time that
these alien invaders are coming.

61
00:10:43,830 --> 00:10:45,400
So you better suit up.

62
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,760
The Volt machines are ready for you.

63
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:49,580
Go.

64
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:50,380
Now.

65
00:11:05,950 --> 00:11:07,090
The aliens have arrived.

66
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:10,370
They are vicious and heartless.

67
00:11:11,390 --> 00:11:14,610
They have caused major destruction all
over the globe.

68
00:11:15,430 --> 00:11:17,670
You must defeat and destroy them.

69
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:23,010
All the military forces of the world are
waiting for you.

70
00:11:24,410 --> 00:11:27,870
Voltess team, you are the last line of
defense.

71
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:30,850
The whole world will be in danger if this
happens.

72
00:11:31,570 --> 00:11:33,710
And this will be the end of humankind.

73
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:42,900
This cannot happen.

74
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,940
Do everything you can to save our planet.

75
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:59,100
Everyone, to your battle stations.

76
00:12:29,130 --> 00:12:30,390
Kids, take care.

77
00:12:32,190 --> 00:12:33,190
Be good.

78
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:34,430
Be brave.

79
00:12:34,970 --> 00:12:35,190
Be...

80
00:12:35,190 --> 00:12:35,650
Be safe.

81
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:36,970
Yes, Ma.

82
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:40,850
Mark, Jamie, take care.

83
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:43,270
Little John.

84
00:12:47,910 --> 00:12:49,650
Marianne, we're running out of time.

85
00:12:50,110 --> 00:12:50,450
Let's go.

86
00:12:56,490 --> 00:12:58,710
Mark, you're number two.

87
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:01,810
Steve, you're number one.

88
00:13:01,810 --> 00:13:02,430
Okay.

89
00:13:03,310 --> 00:13:04,850
Big Bert, number three.

90
00:13:05,170 --> 00:13:05,610
Okay, Ma.

91
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:07,630
Little John, number four.

92
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:08,130
Roger.

93
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:09,730
Jamie, five.

94
00:13:10,350 --> 00:13:10,630
Roger.

95
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,850
Launch conveyors, now.

96
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:16,530
Attention, all machines.

97
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:20,170
Excuse me, we don't have all the controls
here yet.

98
00:14:21,090 --> 00:14:23,370
Can you give us like five minutes?

99
00:14:23,710 --> 00:14:26,430
The controls of that is similar to the
flight simulator.

100
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:27,690
Steve, what else?

101
00:14:28,210 --> 00:14:29,530
It's all just the same.

102
00:14:29,530 --> 00:14:32,070
Steve, take command.

103
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:33,350
Mark.

104
00:14:33,770 --> 00:14:39,080
Big Bert, you handle weaponry and
armaments.

105
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:41,960
Jamie, medical and communication.

106
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,600
Little John.

107
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:45,020
Do what you do best.

108
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:46,340
Engineering.

109
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,260
Copy that, best friend.

110
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,220
Five.

111
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:57,200
Four.

112
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,320
Three.

113
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,180
Two.

114
00:15:05,570 --> 00:15:06,030
Launch.

115
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:23,790
Ah!

116
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:31,390
Easy, boy, easy.

117
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:31,970
Mark.

118
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:32,950
That's not a horse.

119
00:15:42,950 --> 00:15:44,350
Little John, are you okay?

120
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:48,470
Huh?

121
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:55,080
Wait, how did you know?

122
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:57,860
Jamie.

123
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:05,320
Guys, do you see the weapons list?

124
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:07,840
The weapons list?

125
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:11,260
Fort, bazooka, chain knuckles.

126
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:16,540
Oh, ultra electromagnetic whip.

127
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,860
Big Bert, did you just say whip?

128
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:22,320
Yeehaw!

129
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,680
Let's go get the million.

130
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:27,460
Guys, guys, guys, get your head in the
game.

131
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:30,440
What is the medical condition of the team?

132
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:34,460
Captain Fowler reporting all five biosigns
of all team members are okay.

133
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:55,710
Holy.

134
00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:57,710
There's a lot of them.

135
00:16:58,370 --> 00:16:58,830
Wow.

136
00:16:59,770 --> 00:17:01,010
Lin, wow.

137
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:03,550
Lim, can we handle these guys?

138
00:17:03,870 --> 00:17:04,930
It's too late.

139
00:17:05,450 --> 00:17:06,210
We won't make it.

140
00:17:06,930 --> 00:17:08,810
Lim, don't be afraid.

141
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:12,430
Remember, the whole world is counting on
us.

142
00:17:13,510 --> 00:17:14,310
Brother is right.

143
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:15,190
There's no time to lose.

144
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:16,290
Let's go.

145
00:17:17,810 --> 00:17:19,250
Little John, please.

146
00:17:19,250 --> 00:17:21,130
Don't mess up again, okay?

147
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,670
I'll follow you, okay?

148
00:17:23,190 --> 00:17:23,970
Yes, brother.

149
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:25,770
Mama, don't worry.

150
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:28,730
Of course, I'll worry.

151
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:30,310
You don't have enough training.

152
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:33,070
Mama, I can do this.

153
00:17:33,210 --> 00:17:34,690
This is just a video game.

154
00:17:35,230 --> 00:17:36,890
What video game?

155
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:38,430
Oh, my God.

156
00:17:39,430 --> 00:17:40,130
Team,

157
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:44,880
let's engage.

158
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:45,500
Commit, commit.

159
00:17:55,330 --> 00:17:56,650
Use your weapons.

160
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:59,930
Most of the controls are voice activated.

161
00:18:00,390 --> 00:18:02,330
Oh, cool.

162
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:10,400
Helm boomerang.

163
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,280
Frigate rocket.

164
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:26,300
Ranger missile.

165
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:35,030
Bomber missile.

166
00:18:40,570 --> 00:18:41,710
Lander shuriken.

167
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:52,970
There's no end to the weapons of this
planet.

168
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:56,590
This day will not end.

169
00:18:57,070 --> 00:18:58,730
And we will destroy them.

170
00:18:59,950 --> 00:19:01,550
Let's not be reckless.

171
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:05,450
We will not be defeated by war.

172
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:06,910
You're crazy, Draco.

173
00:19:07,870 --> 00:19:09,590
They don't have a chance against our army.

174
00:19:11,090 --> 00:19:12,650
There's still a lack of hard work.

175
00:19:13,510 --> 00:19:16,950
I want to see everyone on that planet die.

176
00:19:16,950 --> 00:19:17,130
What is that?

177
00:19:18,470 --> 00:19:19,910
Take out our weapons.

178
00:19:20,890 --> 00:19:21,830
Take out Doc O'Gaga.

179
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,040
Do you want to be free, John Frey?

180
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:45,320
Watch how the Terrans will be defeated in
our battle.

181
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:53,180
Sir, we are detecting an alien signature.

182
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,680
This is the first time we've picked up a
signal like this.

183
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:58,240
On screen.

184
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:07,340
Sir, enemy classification.

185
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:10,060
It's a Bosnian beast fighter.

186
00:20:11,930 --> 00:20:14,510
Send me the coordinates of that beast
fighter.

187
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:15,100
Now!

188
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:16,200
Yes, sir.

189
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:30,480
Beast fighter?

190
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:36,340
That's a beautiful name for our army.

191
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,360
Draco, continue your promise.

192
00:21:24,790 --> 00:21:31,170
They will only live longer if they can't
open our weapons.

193
00:21:32,130 --> 00:21:34,610
Sir, new energy signature detected.

194
00:21:35,850 --> 00:21:38,330
Computer identifies it as a beast fighter.

195
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:41,950
Bolstein, the Bosnians have released a
beast fighter.

196
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:44,630
Beast fighter?

197
00:21:45,030 --> 00:21:45,890
What is that?

198
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:57,640
Kaiju!

199
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:13,280
Evasive maneuvers!

200
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:23,460
Now is your better chance to bolt in.

201
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,180
We're going to bolt in the robot?

202
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:27,200
What do we do, Doc?

203
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,420
Bolt in, team.

204
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:31,460
You need to fly in a V formation.

205
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:36,280
Steve, your cruiser should be in the front
and center.

206
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:39,280
From now on, this will be your V
formation.

207
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:39,760
Copy?

208
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:41,800
Copy, Ma'am.

209
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,720
Team, let's V together.

210
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:46,040
V formation now!

211
00:23:11,470 --> 00:23:15,330
Now, you will see a red button next to
your center console.

212
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:20,310
To activate the robot transformation,
push that to start the bolt-in sequence.

213
00:23:20,910 --> 00:23:21,390
Roger that.

214
00:23:23,510 --> 00:23:24,910
Let's bolt in!

215
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:25,280
We're almost there.

216
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:28,880
Let's get our legs together.

217
00:24:30,380 --> 00:24:32,720
We believe in each other.

218
00:24:34,100 --> 00:24:36,760
We're all in this together.

219
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:38,380
We're almost there.

220
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:43,660
We're all in this together.

221
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:50,480
We're almost

222
00:25:16,490 --> 00:25:16,670
there.

223
00:25:16,710 --> 00:25:19,150
Geoffrey, look at this.

224
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:33,110
These Terra Ertl soldiers are
extraordinary.

225
00:25:33,710 --> 00:25:35,530
You lack discipline.

226
00:25:36,690 --> 00:25:41,830
I'm sure they will not defeat Doc O'Gaga.

227
00:26:02,020 --> 00:26:06,200
Draco, let the battle begin.

228
00:26:07,860 --> 00:26:09,820
Now, Geoffrey.

229
00:27:09,940 --> 00:27:10,660
That's their champion.

230
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:17,900
If that's their champion, I'm sure they
will defeat our soldier.

231
00:27:18,860 --> 00:27:19,760
What do they call him?

232
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:23,760
Our beast fighter.

233
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:28,400
The Terra Ertl soldiers are extraordinary.

234
00:27:29,060 --> 00:27:29,640
Draco.

235
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:34,940
Doc O'Gaga, make sure Doc O'Gaga will not
defeat their champion.

236
00:27:37,140 --> 00:27:38,620
Yes, sir.

237
00:27:48,010 --> 00:27:49,350
What do they call him?

238
00:27:49,350 --> 00:27:49,870
Our champion.

239
00:27:53,230 --> 00:27:54,790
Don't worry, Little John.

240
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:56,210
We have trained for this, remember?

241
00:27:56,710 --> 00:27:59,710
Yes, we have trained, but Little John is
not.

242
00:27:59,710 --> 00:28:01,970
We'll be in trouble if something happens
to him.

243
00:28:02,470 --> 00:28:04,150
Nothing bad will happen to me.

244
00:28:04,690 --> 00:28:05,190
Trust me.

245
00:28:05,190 --> 00:28:06,190
Be strong.

246
00:28:07,770 --> 00:28:09,890
Remember, the whole world is in our hands.

247
00:28:10,490 --> 00:28:11,510
That's why we have to win.

248
00:28:12,390 --> 00:28:12,990
Roger.

249
00:29:22,050 --> 00:29:24,330
Draco, I'm getting hot.

250
00:29:25,150 --> 00:29:26,090
Finish him.

251
00:29:27,650 --> 00:29:29,110
Now, Geoffrey.

252
00:29:37,980 --> 00:29:38,780
Ah!

253
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:40,680
Ah!

254
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:44,800
Big Bert!

255
00:29:58,930 --> 00:29:59,990
Big Bert!

256
00:30:00,950 --> 00:30:01,890
Bio warning signs.

257
00:30:02,370 --> 00:30:02,530
Are you okay?

258
00:30:02,990 --> 00:30:03,390
I'm okay.

259
00:30:08,730 --> 00:30:09,530
Oh,

260
00:30:22,790 --> 00:30:22,810
no.

261
00:30:23,350 --> 00:30:24,010
He's strong.

262
00:30:27,510 --> 00:30:29,110
Everyone's bio signs are good.

263
00:30:29,110 --> 00:30:31,750
Little John, are you okay?

264
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:33,090
I'm okay.

265
00:30:33,690 --> 00:30:34,430
I just slipped.

266
00:30:41,140 --> 00:30:42,720
Let's get him back.

267
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:47,000
Weapon recommendation, chain knuckles.

268
00:30:47,460 --> 00:30:47,740
Roger.

269
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:51,920
Chain knuckles!

270
00:31:05,700 --> 00:31:09,240
This is an ultra-electromagnetic weapon.

271
00:31:09,880 --> 00:31:11,620
Mark, that's your specialty.

272
00:31:11,620 --> 00:31:11,940
You can do it.

273
00:31:13,460 --> 00:31:15,760
Ultra-electromagnetic weapon!

274
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:28,010
Ultra-electromagnetic staff!

275
00:31:48,780 --> 00:31:49,580
Yes!

276
00:31:50,060 --> 00:31:50,980
Oh, nice.

277
00:31:54,600 --> 00:31:55,060
Wait.

278
00:31:58,080 --> 00:32:00,920
Why do I feel like we're losing?

279
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,140
Shut up, Zul.

280
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:04,400
No.

281
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:13,720
Let's finish this.

282
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:16,220
Shut up, laser sword.

283
00:32:17,940 --> 00:32:18,960
Shut up.

284
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:21,600
Shut up!

285
00:34:15,100 --> 00:34:15,800
Yay!

286
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:27,080
I can't believe it.

287
00:34:27,080 --> 00:34:29,900
They lost to Doku Gaga.

288
00:34:30,860 --> 00:34:31,280
John.

289
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:43,920
You are a brave warrior.

290
00:34:46,620 --> 00:34:49,590
You may have the advantage now,
Ertugrul.

291
00:34:50,580 --> 00:34:52,740
But the fight is not over yet.

292
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:58,300
There is no planet that can defeat the
mighty Empire of Buzot.

293
00:36:02,710 --> 00:36:03,570
Sir!

294
00:36:05,730 --> 00:36:08,070
Team Voltus V reporting.

295
00:36:10,490 --> 00:36:11,230
Welcome back.

296
00:36:12,590 --> 00:36:13,930
Mission accomplished.

297
00:36:19,980 --> 00:36:22,520
Job well done, Team Voltus V.

298
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:24,880
We are so proud of you.

299
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:27,420
And your parents are waiting for hugs.

300
00:36:28,460 --> 00:36:28,940
Aris!

301
00:36:45,760 --> 00:36:46,680
Prove yourself.

302
00:36:48,500 --> 00:36:49,740
You made me.

303
00:36:52,020 --> 00:36:52,920
Thank you.

304
00:36:58,720 --> 00:37:00,940
Your father will be so proud of you.

305
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:02,640
Good job.

306
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:05,580
Thank you, Dad.

307
00:37:10,040 --> 00:37:10,900
Good job.

308
00:37:16,050 --> 00:37:16,690
Mark.

309
00:37:26,340 --> 00:37:27,860
You did a great job.

310
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:29,980
You made me proud of you.

311
00:37:40,540 --> 00:37:41,440
Thank you.

312
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:47,700
John Frey.

313
00:37:49,230 --> 00:37:49,860
Zardoz.

314
00:37:50,440 --> 00:37:52,460
What's the news on Terra Air 2?

315
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:56,480
I was hoping it would fall into your
hands.

316
00:37:57,770 --> 00:37:58,940
I am sorry.

317
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:00,810
But we are on the same side.

318
00:38:01,740 --> 00:38:03,480
They have a strong army.

319
00:38:03,580 --> 00:38:04,180
Which means?

320
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:08,770
Your army was defeated.

321
00:38:15,020 --> 00:38:16,540
I thought you were good.

322
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:22,800
I thought you were one of the heroes since
you defeated your father.

323
00:38:26,930 --> 00:38:29,770
Aren't you ashamed of my ministers?

324
00:38:29,870 --> 00:38:34,990
Of the people of Busan who idolize you.

325
00:38:39,470 --> 00:38:41,270
Where is your talent?

326
00:38:42,570 --> 00:38:43,470
Your intelligence?

327
00:38:45,130 --> 00:38:47,170
Your courage?

328
00:38:50,660 --> 00:38:52,380
Why were you defeated?

329
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:55,880
Forgive me, John Frey.

330
00:38:57,180 --> 00:38:58,900
I promise you.

331
00:38:59,700 --> 00:39:01,940
I will not go back to Busan.

332
00:39:01,940 --> 00:39:05,420
Until the planet Terra Air 2 is destroyed.

333
00:39:06,080 --> 00:39:06,640
Yes.

334
00:39:07,620 --> 00:39:11,800
Don't come back until you can't do
anything for me.

335
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:16,820
Don't embarrass me, Zardoz.

336
00:39:17,140 --> 00:39:22,340
Don't embarrass yourself like your father,
Sirotgar.

337
00:39:22,860 --> 00:39:25,160
Don't embarrass the whole of Busan.

338
00:39:25,540 --> 00:39:27,240
Najmi Imperium.

339
00:40:09,690 --> 00:40:10,010
Dad.

340
00:40:11,190 --> 00:40:11,870
Mom.

341
00:40:12,070 --> 00:40:14,630
We know you are angry.

342
00:40:15,850 --> 00:40:16,850
You are afraid.

343
00:40:18,690 --> 00:40:20,210
Especially little John.

344
00:40:21,810 --> 00:40:22,830
You are three, son.

345
00:40:23,910 --> 00:40:25,110
What if you were defeated?

346
00:40:26,690 --> 00:40:29,370
Then all three of you will be gone from
me.

347
00:40:29,910 --> 00:40:32,990
But what happened is not what you are
afraid of, Mom.

348
00:40:33,770 --> 00:40:34,330
Mom.

349
00:40:35,810 --> 00:40:36,150
Trust.

350
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:39,030
We trust you.

351
00:40:40,010 --> 00:40:40,490
You, Papa.

352
00:40:41,490 --> 00:40:42,370
Dr. Smith.

353
00:40:43,610 --> 00:40:46,850
That's why we have the confidence to fight
using the Voltis robot.

354
00:40:47,510 --> 00:40:49,010
Because we know what you did.

355
00:40:49,950 --> 00:40:50,890
Trust, Mom.

356
00:40:52,210 --> 00:40:53,290
That's why, Mom.

357
00:40:55,070 --> 00:40:58,030
Mom, you should trust your father's
creations.

358
00:41:00,230 --> 00:41:02,150
And you should trust your children.

359
00:41:03,190 --> 00:41:03,990
Yes, Mom.

360
00:41:04,530 --> 00:41:05,990
That's why you should let me go.

361
00:41:06,370 --> 00:41:08,210
Because we need the whole world.

362
00:41:08,210 --> 00:41:10,650
We are your gift to our planet.

363
00:41:15,180 --> 00:41:17,160
Be careful, children.

364
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:20,920
Don't let anything bad happen to you.

365
00:41:21,680 --> 00:41:22,160
Promise.

366
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:43,660
I can't believe that we were defeated by
the Terra Air 2 because of the Voltis 5.

367
00:41:44,180 --> 00:41:45,100
Don't worry.

368
00:41:45,380 --> 00:41:48,480
I'm studying about their main weapon.

369
00:41:54,690 --> 00:41:55,490
Draco.

370
00:41:56,730 --> 00:41:58,090
What are you investigating?

371
00:42:00,030 --> 00:42:07,890
I'm just wondering how the Terra Air 2 got
this technology from the Voltis 5.

372
00:42:10,510 --> 00:42:14,530
I'm sure that it's not from their planet.

373
00:42:24,120 --> 00:42:28,860
Is there a way to find out where the
Terras hide their weapons?

374
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:34,480
That's what the Minister wants to know.

375
00:42:35,380 --> 00:42:37,960
Let's just wait for his surprise.

376
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:38,820
Wait.

377
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:41,160
Can't we know everything?

378
00:42:42,020 --> 00:42:43,040
Why is Zul here?

379
00:42:43,380 --> 00:42:43,900
Zul.

380
00:42:45,200 --> 00:42:45,640
What do you want?

381
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:48,120
Next time, dear Prince.

382
00:43:00,170 --> 00:43:01,990
Why is it dark here?

383
00:43:03,110 --> 00:43:03,790
Surprise!

384
00:43:07,290 --> 00:43:09,330
Thank you, but it's my birthday tomorrow.

385
00:43:09,990 --> 00:43:10,990
What's going on, Mom?

386
00:43:11,070 --> 00:43:11,770
You seem to be in a hurry.

387
00:43:13,030 --> 00:43:17,530
And if we're going to do everything
tomorrow, then it's not a surprise

388
00:43:17,530 --> 00:43:17,690
anymore.

389
00:43:19,010 --> 00:43:20,530
Don't call it a surprise.

390
00:43:21,190 --> 00:43:22,210
Blow your candle.

391
00:43:26,200 --> 00:43:28,100
One, two, wish.

392
00:43:29,120 --> 00:43:30,160
Wish first.

393
00:43:31,360 --> 00:43:33,440
Well, I want all of us to blow the candle.

394
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:36,320
I want to share my birthday luck with all
of you.

395
00:43:36,860 --> 00:43:37,240
Go ahead.

396
00:43:37,660 --> 00:43:42,500
One, two, three.

397
00:43:45,980 --> 00:43:46,760
What's your wish?

398
00:43:47,740 --> 00:43:50,340
Well, I don't have a wish for myself
anymore.

399
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:54,280
So, my wish is that you are always safe.

400
00:43:55,440 --> 00:43:57,620
And that your wishes will come true.

401
00:43:58,320 --> 00:44:00,100
You know what I always say.

402
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:03,100
Be strong, be brave, be safe.

403
00:44:06,480 --> 00:44:10,680
So, it means that my wish will come true.

404
00:44:13,160 --> 00:44:15,640
You know, I have a wish too.

405
00:44:15,640 --> 00:44:16,520
Really, son?

406
00:44:16,660 --> 00:44:17,720
You have a crush on Jamie?

407
00:44:19,420 --> 00:44:21,540
These are all fake news.

408
00:44:22,200 --> 00:44:23,140
Don't believe them.

409
00:44:23,980 --> 00:44:25,040
Mom is just stressed.

410
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:28,980
Hey, that's enough.

411
00:44:29,320 --> 00:44:30,280
You might get into a fight.

412
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:33,300
Steve, you're the older brother.

413
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:35,080
You shouldn't hurt your siblings.

414
00:44:36,060 --> 00:44:36,500
Yes, ma'am.

415
00:44:36,920 --> 00:44:39,460
And you two, don't tease your siblings too
much.

416
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:42,080
Let's eat.

417
00:44:42,340 --> 00:44:43,000
Let's eat this.

418
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:43,400
Hurry up.

419
00:44:44,500 --> 00:44:45,140
Okay,

420
00:44:48,560 --> 00:44:50,060
one, two, three.

421
00:44:51,340 --> 00:44:53,620
How big is Big Bird?

422
00:44:53,760 --> 00:44:54,820
Half of it is Big Bird.

423
00:45:01,480 --> 00:45:02,120
Zul!

424
00:45:03,460 --> 00:45:04,780
Where is Voltes Five?

425
00:45:06,200 --> 00:45:07,080
You've been looking for him since
yesterday.

426
00:45:07,220 --> 00:45:07,600
I'm getting hot.

427
00:45:09,180 --> 00:45:10,060
What's going on?

428
00:45:10,560 --> 00:45:13,160
Principal Sandoz, this is what I want to
show you.

429
00:45:15,160 --> 00:45:20,700
I've been told that there's a strong
energy coming from that island.

430
00:45:21,440 --> 00:45:28,960
There's a strong signal that the defense
of Terra Ertube is in danger.

431
00:45:33,390 --> 00:45:36,470
Voltes Five is probably hiding there.

432
00:45:44,140 --> 00:45:45,440
Terra Ertube people are smart.

433
00:45:46,260 --> 00:45:48,340
They put their camp on a hidden island.

434
00:45:50,020 --> 00:45:52,280
But they haven't been able to hide from
us.

435
00:45:52,700 --> 00:45:54,720
When are you going to attack, Jomfre?

436
00:45:55,880 --> 00:45:56,480
We're just waiting for your budget.

437
00:46:01,270 --> 00:46:03,350
Is our Beast Fighter ready?

438
00:46:03,870 --> 00:46:05,010
He's ready, Jomfre.

439
00:46:07,210 --> 00:46:08,510
I want to meet him.

440
00:46:09,310 --> 00:46:09,730
Sibar!

441
00:46:12,430 --> 00:46:15,550
I'm introducing our new champion.

442
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:20,380
That's Baizanga.

443
00:46:20,380 --> 00:46:25,320
Baizanga, contact Voltes Five so that we
can destroy this planet.

444
00:46:28,380 --> 00:46:29,220
Baizanga...

445
00:46:30,610 --> 00:46:32,950
I'm looking forward to meeting you.

446
00:46:42,400 --> 00:46:50,180
You are all chosen to defend our planet
Earth from Bosanian invasion.

447
00:46:52,320 --> 00:46:54,800
Are you ready to defend our planet?

448
00:46:55,560 --> 00:46:56,380
Yes, sir!

449
00:47:00,330 --> 00:47:01,730
Voltes Five team...

450
00:47:03,550 --> 00:47:07,730
because of your extraordinary skills and
abilities...

451
00:47:09,090 --> 00:47:10,790
and your personal destinies...

452
00:47:11,990 --> 00:47:14,530
you are the last defense of this planet.

453
00:47:16,310 --> 00:47:19,910
Should other defense plans fail...

454
00:47:21,620 --> 00:47:22,600
we are counting on you.

455
00:47:23,620 --> 00:47:25,120
Do you include the medical team?

456
00:47:26,180 --> 00:47:27,460
All of us...

457
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:34,080
should aim to achieve the highest
standards of battle.

458
00:47:39,430 --> 00:47:42,270
Anything less is not acceptable.

459
00:47:46,640 --> 00:47:50,440
So today, prepare yourselves...

460
00:47:50,440 --> 00:47:54,660
for we are going to implement a critical
test.

461
00:47:56,700 --> 00:48:00,900
The Voltes Five team shall openly attack
the camp...

462
00:48:00,900 --> 00:48:02,720
as though they are Bosanians.

463
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:05,540
And the Voltes Five team shall
counter-attack the camp...

464
00:48:05,540 --> 00:48:07,480
as though they are real alien invaders.

465
00:48:09,940 --> 00:48:11,760
We will be using live ammunitions.

466
00:48:13,140 --> 00:48:15,140
Turn off safety protocols.

467
00:48:17,300 --> 00:48:19,720
The Voltes Five team shall try this
drill...

468
00:48:21,700 --> 00:48:24,600
and the Camping Falcon's strategy for
defense.

469
00:48:25,700 --> 00:48:26,480
Are there any questions?

470
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:28,160
No safety protocols?

471
00:48:28,720 --> 00:48:30,500
So if we get hit, game over?

472
00:48:30,500 --> 00:48:30,620
No, sir.

473
00:48:31,420 --> 00:48:32,900
Live ammunition...

474
00:48:32,900 --> 00:48:34,080
Kaboom!

475
00:48:34,280 --> 00:48:34,720
We're dead.

476
00:48:36,640 --> 00:48:37,280
Team...

477
00:48:37,280 --> 00:48:41,200
this drill will help us prepare
ourselves...

478
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:44,040
in case of an actual Bosanian attack.

479
00:48:45,500 --> 00:48:46,780
That's why...

480
00:48:46,780 --> 00:48:48,320
all of us...

481
00:48:48,320 --> 00:48:49,640
should do our best.

482
00:48:50,400 --> 00:48:51,080
Yes, sir.

483
00:48:52,260 --> 00:48:53,320
We are ready.

484
00:48:56,160 --> 00:48:56,800
Everyone...

485
00:48:56,800 --> 00:48:58,060
prepare for live weapons drill.

486
00:48:58,060 --> 00:48:59,820
To your stations.

487
00:49:01,020 --> 00:49:01,320
Attention.

488
00:49:02,100 --> 00:49:03,960
All crew will check the screening on the
tower.

489
00:49:05,980 --> 00:49:06,280
Extra...

490
00:49:06,580 --> 00:49:08,040
this is not just a simple drill.

491
00:49:08,820 --> 00:49:09,220
And?

492
00:49:09,900 --> 00:49:12,540
So you don't trust your training since we
were kids?

493
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:16,380
I don't have much training, sir.

494
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:18,440
Guys, we got this.

495
00:49:18,640 --> 00:49:20,400
We already defeated the enemy,
right?

496
00:49:20,480 --> 00:49:21,300
We already did this.

497
00:49:21,480 --> 00:49:24,040
What does Mama always say?

498
00:49:25,020 --> 00:49:25,900
Be brave.

499
00:49:25,900 --> 00:49:27,180
Be strong.

500
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:28,680
Be brave.

501
00:49:28,960 --> 00:49:29,740
Be strong.

502
00:49:59,220 --> 00:49:59,980
You know what to do.

503
00:50:00,860 --> 00:50:02,100
Let the battle begin.

504
00:50:10,380 --> 00:50:11,600
Pattern Delta.

505
00:50:15,340 --> 00:50:16,280
Attack commencing.

506
00:50:16,700 --> 00:50:17,480
Watch out, guys.

507
00:50:30,380 --> 00:50:31,200
Here and there.

508
00:50:31,760 --> 00:50:32,460
Focus.

509
00:50:40,090 --> 00:50:41,610
Alright, countermeasures.

510
00:50:47,210 --> 00:50:48,610
Good job, all this team.

511
00:50:48,610 --> 00:50:51,210
You think you can beat us?

512
00:50:52,810 --> 00:50:54,970
Let's see what they're made of.

513
00:50:55,490 --> 00:50:57,770
Launch Falcon Missiles.

514
00:50:58,010 --> 00:50:58,630
Full spreads.

515
00:51:10,820 --> 00:51:12,140
Sky heroes in.

516
00:51:16,050 --> 00:51:21,710
This is where the unique energy I'm
talking about comes from, Prince Vesados.

517
00:51:29,260 --> 00:51:30,600
General Draco.

518
00:51:32,020 --> 00:51:33,100
Begin the attack.

519
00:51:52,640 --> 00:51:53,120
Nice.

520
00:51:53,120 --> 00:51:55,260
Who was the direct hit on your cap?

521
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:57,460
Not me.

522
00:51:58,180 --> 00:51:58,440
Me.

523
00:51:59,380 --> 00:52:00,540
Especially me.

524
00:52:01,160 --> 00:52:02,840
If it wasn't one of us, who was it from?

525
00:52:03,720 --> 00:52:04,400
Wait, wait.

526
00:52:13,550 --> 00:52:15,410
Bosan energy signature confirmed.

527
00:52:15,990 --> 00:52:17,170
The Bosanians are back.

528
00:52:31,710 --> 00:52:32,770
Battle stations, everyone.

529
00:52:33,570 --> 00:52:34,230
Aye, aye, sir.

530
00:52:34,710 --> 00:52:36,220
CBF defense protocol activated.

531
00:52:36,220 --> 00:52:36,880
Activated.

532
00:52:42,590 --> 00:52:44,050
Tactical station reports ready.

533
00:52:44,690 --> 00:52:45,970
Engineering station ready.

534
00:52:46,370 --> 00:52:47,970
Medical and life support reports ready.

535
00:53:02,540 --> 00:53:03,780
It's a beast fighter.

536
00:53:07,140 --> 00:53:09,360
Team, get ready for the real battle.

537
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:10,940
Let's go.

538
00:53:16,630 --> 00:53:18,470
Don't let him get close to the camp.

539
00:53:19,050 --> 00:53:20,770
And don't give him a chance to retaliate.

540
00:53:20,990 --> 00:53:21,170
Roger.

541
00:53:23,950 --> 00:53:25,250
Richard, you have the control.

542
00:53:25,550 --> 00:53:26,930
I'm flying back to EDF headquarters.

543
00:53:27,450 --> 00:53:28,150
I'll speed Oscar.

544
00:53:28,390 --> 00:53:31,070
Chief Kelly, once I'm out, raise your
shields.

545
00:53:31,450 --> 00:53:32,070
Aye, aye, sir.

546
00:53:36,140 --> 00:53:37,260
Claw, boomerang!

547
00:53:41,840 --> 00:53:42,900
Bomber, missile!

548
00:53:45,000 --> 00:53:46,380
Lander, missile!

549
00:53:47,260 --> 00:53:48,380
Lander, missile!

550
00:53:49,500 --> 00:53:50,540
Frigate, missiles!

551
00:53:57,210 --> 00:53:58,290
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

552
00:53:58,790 --> 00:53:59,650
Watch out, watch out!

553
00:54:00,870 --> 00:54:01,630
Mark, rig left!

554
00:54:10,900 --> 00:54:11,840
This guy is too much.

555
00:54:14,740 --> 00:54:15,780
He's still standing.

556
00:54:16,440 --> 00:54:17,780
It's like he wasn't hit.

557
00:54:18,140 --> 00:54:19,900
You just didn't hit our missiles.

558
00:54:20,840 --> 00:54:22,020
It's scary.

559
00:54:22,840 --> 00:54:24,200
And he's not our enemy.

560
00:54:30,520 --> 00:54:33,260
Commander Robinson, helicopter is clear
from base.

561
00:54:36,100 --> 00:54:37,120
Activating shields.

562
00:54:48,140 --> 00:54:49,840
I can't believe this.

563
00:54:50,660 --> 00:54:54,940
No matter what the Volt is doing,
the beast fighter doesn't seem to be

564
00:54:54,940 --> 00:54:54,940
affected.

565
00:55:04,600 --> 00:55:06,460
Commander Robinson, what's going on?

566
00:55:07,120 --> 00:55:08,720
Marianne, I can barely hear you.

567
00:55:09,980 --> 00:55:10,960
I'm out of CBF.

568
00:55:11,400 --> 00:55:12,400
Hello, Marianne?

569
00:55:12,800 --> 00:55:13,640
Commander Robinson?

570
00:55:15,080 --> 00:55:15,740
Hello?

571
00:55:16,680 --> 00:55:17,020
Hello?

572
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:21,880
Patch me to Captain Valcom.

573
00:55:22,240 --> 00:55:22,740
Copy, sir.

574
00:55:24,780 --> 00:55:25,340
Yes, Commander?

575
00:55:26,200 --> 00:55:27,640
Has anyone seen Marianne?

576
00:55:29,020 --> 00:55:30,820
She was trying to call me when the line
was cut.

577
00:55:31,360 --> 00:55:33,420
I'm sure she's already warning her
children.

578
00:55:34,060 --> 00:55:34,800
Sergeant Major?

579
00:55:36,340 --> 00:55:36,740
Sir?

580
00:55:38,560 --> 00:55:39,720
Marianne Armstrong, now.

581
00:55:40,040 --> 00:55:40,740
Copy that, sir.

582
00:55:49,540 --> 00:55:50,640
Master Chief, hurry up.

583
00:55:50,740 --> 00:55:52,700
We need to reach the headquarters as fast
as we can.

584
00:55:53,820 --> 00:55:54,460
Copy, Doc.

585
00:55:56,940 --> 00:55:57,420
Security!

586
00:55:58,160 --> 00:55:59,540
Back to CBF immediately!

587
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:00,380
Next alert!

588
00:56:11,290 --> 00:56:12,170
Oh, my God!

589
00:56:12,830 --> 00:56:13,570
What's going on?

590
00:56:55,460 --> 00:56:55,940
All right!

591
00:56:57,380 --> 00:56:59,240
Destroy everything that attacks us!

592
00:57:36,370 --> 00:57:37,770
Protect Camp Atolcos!

593
00:57:38,270 --> 00:57:38,850
Team, attack!

594
00:57:54,980 --> 00:57:55,960
Evade and maneuver!

595
00:58:09,870 --> 00:58:10,490
What?

596
00:58:10,730 --> 00:58:12,470
Are we going to lose to him?

597
00:58:12,950 --> 00:58:13,670
Leave it to me.

598
00:58:19,640 --> 00:58:20,860
Bomber in!

599
00:58:45,420 --> 00:58:47,580
We need to help the Baltis team.

600
00:58:48,160 --> 00:58:48,660
I agree.

601
00:58:49,320 --> 00:58:52,380
Chief, arm Hawk missiles.

602
00:58:53,640 --> 00:58:54,260
On!

603
00:58:54,700 --> 00:58:55,680
On my signal.

604
00:59:06,810 --> 00:59:07,810
Engage, full attack!

605
00:59:11,520 --> 00:59:12,200
Load!

606
00:59:12,760 --> 00:59:13,500
Missiles away!

607
00:59:27,470 --> 00:59:28,030
Finish him!

608
00:59:29,090 --> 00:59:30,750
Next alert!

609
00:59:42,060 --> 00:59:42,740
Doctor!

610
00:59:43,340 --> 00:59:45,040
Tactical detects enemy approaching!

611
00:59:52,510 --> 00:59:54,850
What on earth is that?

612
01:00:17,560 --> 01:00:19,200
Oh, that's creepy.

613
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:21,500
What is it?

614
01:00:23,000 --> 01:00:24,120
It's a skull.

615
01:00:29,600 --> 01:00:30,900
A symbol of death.

616
01:00:32,500 --> 01:00:33,780
A sign to intimidate.

617
01:00:34,720 --> 01:00:35,620
Psych warfare.

618
01:00:36,820 --> 01:00:39,140
It might be another beast fighter.

619
01:00:40,820 --> 01:00:44,540
Whatever it is, hopefully he won't be able
to penetrate the barrier of Camp Big Pac.

620
01:00:55,500 --> 01:00:57,200
Now the real fun begins.

621
01:01:04,210 --> 01:01:04,870
Let's fight!

622
01:01:11,400 --> 01:01:12,200
Oh, Pasugod!

623
01:01:14,540 --> 01:01:15,240
This one is a beast!

624
01:01:18,020 --> 01:01:19,060
Brace for impact!

625
01:01:39,330 --> 01:01:41,150
You think you're strong?

626
01:02:13,950 --> 01:02:15,030
Baltis, bazooka!

627
01:02:37,320 --> 01:02:38,460
Yes, chief!

628
01:02:51,100 --> 01:02:52,160
Dr. Armstrong?

629
01:02:53,400 --> 01:02:54,700
Marianne, Marianne!

630
01:02:55,520 --> 01:02:56,420
It's dangerous here.

631
01:02:57,840 --> 01:02:58,500
Let's move!

632
01:02:58,840 --> 01:02:59,040
Move!

633
01:02:59,720 --> 01:02:59,920
Move!

634
01:03:09,520 --> 01:03:11,540
Oh no, the barrier is activated.

635
01:03:11,900 --> 01:03:12,560
We won't be able to enter.

636
01:03:14,220 --> 01:03:15,060
Hmm.

637
01:03:16,720 --> 01:03:17,100
What a pity.

638
01:03:19,360 --> 01:03:21,780
We won't be able to return to their nest.

639
01:03:24,640 --> 01:03:26,140
Because of that.

640
01:03:26,720 --> 01:03:28,000
They also made a mess.

641
01:03:30,420 --> 01:03:34,020
Why are you pitying such a lowly creature?

642
01:03:35,160 --> 01:03:36,860
Call Dr. Smith.

643
01:03:36,880 --> 01:03:37,620
We're outside.

644
01:03:37,940 --> 01:03:38,780
Right.

645
01:03:40,300 --> 01:03:41,780
Please, don't be stupid.

646
01:03:41,940 --> 01:03:42,400
Not now.

647
01:03:42,520 --> 01:03:42,880
Please!

648
01:03:48,540 --> 01:03:49,580
Dr. Smith!

649
01:03:50,160 --> 01:03:51,180
Hello, Dr. Smith!

650
01:03:51,300 --> 01:03:51,520
Richard!

651
01:03:52,160 --> 01:03:52,400
Hello!

652
01:03:57,100 --> 01:03:57,740
General Drak.

653
01:04:01,370 --> 01:04:02,370
Play this one.

654
01:04:27,630 --> 01:04:29,510
Let's see if you can still escape.

655
01:04:36,120 --> 01:04:36,840
Marianne!

656
01:04:50,980 --> 01:04:51,920
Master Chief!

657
01:04:53,800 --> 01:04:55,920
Master Chief, we need to get out of here!

658
01:04:57,740 --> 01:04:58,720
Master Chief!

659
01:05:02,350 --> 01:05:03,030
Master Chief!

660
01:05:05,350 --> 01:05:06,450
Master Chief!

661
01:05:12,590 --> 01:05:13,990
Commander, look.

662
01:05:15,010 --> 01:05:16,690
The game we're playing is still alive.

663
01:05:17,730 --> 01:05:19,170
Do you want me to finish it?

664
01:05:30,670 --> 01:05:30,710
No!

665
01:05:33,600 --> 01:05:34,570
Wait a minute.

666
01:05:35,160 --> 01:05:36,410
What is she doing?

667
01:05:37,310 --> 01:05:38,330
This one is brave.

668
01:05:40,090 --> 01:05:41,910
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

669
01:05:43,050 --> 01:05:44,230
This creature is crazy.

670
01:05:53,570 --> 01:05:54,750
Ah!

671
01:06:00,760 --> 01:06:01,350
Ah!

672
01:06:07,090 --> 01:06:08,630
She threw us.

673
01:06:09,990 --> 01:06:10,090
Ah!

674
01:06:12,890 --> 01:06:14,070
You're crazy!

675
01:06:14,770 --> 01:06:15,250
You're crazy.

676
01:06:16,370 --> 01:06:16,990
You're crazy.

677
01:06:16,990 --> 01:06:20,170
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

678
01:06:21,530 --> 01:06:21,930
Ah!

679
01:06:24,150 --> 01:06:25,670
She has a strong body.

680
01:06:25,950 --> 01:06:29,130
She has a strong duty to the forces of the
terrorists.

681
01:06:29,990 --> 01:06:31,350
That's why she's brave.

682
01:06:35,510 --> 01:06:37,390
She needs to be killed.

683
01:07:24,860 --> 01:07:29,900
All this team, you need to kill that beast
fighter and proceed immediately to Camp

684
01:07:29,900 --> 01:07:30,340
Big Falcon.

685
01:07:30,940 --> 01:07:32,920
There's another alien entity threatening
the camp.

686
01:07:33,940 --> 01:07:34,580
We need you back.

687
01:07:35,270 --> 01:07:36,460
We need you back in CDF.

688
01:07:39,630 --> 01:07:41,750
You have fallen into the trap of the
enemy.

689
01:07:43,350 --> 01:07:44,230
You are under attack.

690
01:07:46,170 --> 01:07:47,170
Your mother is hurt.

691
01:07:47,790 --> 01:07:47,950
What?

692
01:07:49,250 --> 01:07:51,210
My mother is hurt?

693
01:07:52,230 --> 01:07:53,590
Brother, let's go back now.

694
01:07:53,590 --> 01:07:55,490
How is my mother?

695
01:07:55,870 --> 01:07:56,450
Is she critical?

696
01:07:58,830 --> 01:07:59,750
We don't know.

697
01:08:00,450 --> 01:08:02,750
She's outside the barrier and we can't
lift the barrier.

698
01:08:03,790 --> 01:08:05,570
The CBF will be compromised.

699
01:08:06,610 --> 01:08:07,330
We need you here.

700
01:08:08,270 --> 01:08:08,610
Roger.

701
01:08:18,710 --> 01:08:19,270
Wait.

702
01:08:20,630 --> 01:08:21,550
Where's the enemy?

703
01:08:21,830 --> 01:08:22,370
He's scared.

704
01:08:22,570 --> 01:08:23,050
He's hiding.

705
01:08:23,630 --> 01:08:26,070
Let's go back to the camp.

706
01:08:26,190 --> 01:08:26,730
No, no, no.

707
01:08:28,090 --> 01:08:28,970
He's just hiding.

708
01:08:28,970 --> 01:08:33,110
We need to find him so he won't bother us
again.

709
01:08:33,370 --> 01:08:34,970
But brother, what about my mother?

710
01:08:36,070 --> 01:08:37,650
Brother, I'm just worried about my mother.

711
01:08:37,730 --> 01:08:38,830
We need to find her.

712
01:08:39,370 --> 01:08:40,610
Steve Bigbert is right, okay?

713
01:08:41,350 --> 01:08:43,270
This is just part of the strategy of the
beast fighter.

714
01:08:43,410 --> 01:08:43,750
It will come out.

715
01:08:44,710 --> 01:08:46,790
We're far stronger than this beast
fighter.

716
01:08:47,830 --> 01:08:50,210
Whatever his strategy is, we will defeat
him.

717
01:08:51,350 --> 01:08:52,230
Let's follow him.

718
01:08:52,550 --> 01:08:54,430
We need to go back to the camp now.

719
01:09:10,890 --> 01:09:11,890
Has Marianne been rescued?

720
01:09:13,950 --> 01:09:16,550
Oscar, I'm going to try my best to rescue
her.

721
01:09:16,830 --> 01:09:19,450
I'm just waiting for the right opportunity
to get her.

722
01:09:45,590 --> 01:09:48,370
CBF command, we found Dr. Armstrong.

723
01:09:49,470 --> 01:09:50,390
Retrieving her now.

724
01:09:56,220 --> 01:09:57,820
We're going to look for the beast fighter.

725
01:09:58,440 --> 01:09:58,980
Brother, don't.

726
01:09:59,860 --> 01:10:00,960
My mother needs us.

727
01:10:02,020 --> 01:10:03,100
Let's go back to the camp.

728
01:10:03,460 --> 01:10:05,380
But brother, I don't want to.

729
01:10:05,720 --> 01:10:06,860
Let's go back to our mother.

730
01:10:06,860 --> 01:10:08,560
No, little John.

731
01:10:08,720 --> 01:10:10,180
We need to find the beast fighter.

732
01:10:10,900 --> 01:10:14,260
Because if we don't destroy him now,
he will come back later.

733
01:10:14,480 --> 01:10:15,340
But what about his mother?

734
01:10:15,560 --> 01:10:17,540
Didn't she say that his right hand is not
strong?

735
01:10:18,180 --> 01:10:20,140
Don't you care what he's wearing now?

736
01:10:20,640 --> 01:10:21,660
Maybe he's wearing something else.

737
01:10:22,020 --> 01:10:22,600
Let's vault out.

738
01:10:23,060 --> 01:10:23,540
Agreed.

739
01:10:23,820 --> 01:10:25,200
We're preparing to vault out.

740
01:10:25,740 --> 01:10:28,900
Bigbert, little John, listen to me.

741
01:10:30,380 --> 01:10:31,940
We can't vault out now.

742
01:10:32,340 --> 01:10:36,160
Because if we split up, we won't be able
to secure the base.

743
01:10:36,860 --> 01:10:36,960
Okay?

744
01:10:37,900 --> 01:10:39,440
More lives could be at risk.

745
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:44,870
Our mission is to protect the whole world.

746
01:10:45,610 --> 01:10:45,750
Huh?

747
01:10:55,900 --> 01:10:58,820
Captain, sir, activate hologram
transmission.

748
01:10:59,360 --> 01:10:59,680
Aye, sir.

749
01:11:05,520 --> 01:11:07,960
Sir, incoming hologram transmission.

750
01:11:13,320 --> 01:11:15,320
Dr. Smith, what's happening in the camp?

751
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:20,040
Our defense missiles are going to match
against the Skull Ship.

752
01:11:20,700 --> 01:11:22,220
Jet fighters are all shut down.

753
01:11:23,120 --> 01:11:24,280
CBF is in danger.

754
01:11:25,480 --> 01:11:27,080
Our force field barriers are about to be
compromised.

755
01:11:28,580 --> 01:11:30,200
I'll see if I can send more
reinforcements.

756
01:11:30,420 --> 01:11:31,320
That would be a great help.

757
01:11:31,600 --> 01:11:31,780
Go!

758
01:11:37,080 --> 01:11:39,640
Captain, sir, email Global Statute Report.

759
01:11:40,140 --> 01:11:40,640
Copy, sir.

760
01:11:44,510 --> 01:11:45,340
How's her condition?

761
01:11:45,590 --> 01:11:47,090
Doc, it looks like she has internal
injuries.

762
01:11:48,240 --> 01:11:49,400
Marianne, can you hear me?

763
01:11:50,400 --> 01:11:51,270
Yes, son.

764
01:11:52,220 --> 01:11:53,820
Don't worry, everything will be okay.

765
01:11:54,200 --> 01:11:55,720
They're on their way back to the base.

766
01:11:55,980 --> 01:11:56,180
Okay?

767
01:11:56,560 --> 01:11:57,240
It will be okay.

768
01:11:57,380 --> 01:11:58,380
Doc, we have to hurry.

769
01:11:59,090 --> 01:12:00,430
Go, go, go, go, go, go!

770
01:12:32,430 --> 01:12:37,030
You didn't tell me that our fight against
the Terra Air Force would be easy.

771
01:12:37,610 --> 01:12:39,050
You're right, John Fred.

772
01:12:40,090 --> 01:12:41,430
We prepared them too much.

773
01:12:43,110 --> 01:12:43,510
Draco!

774
01:12:43,510 --> 01:12:43,590
Doc!

775
01:12:44,490 --> 01:12:46,530
Just keep doing what you're doing.

776
01:12:47,350 --> 01:12:49,670
I'm happy watching you.

777
01:12:52,990 --> 01:12:53,550
Doc!

778
01:12:54,070 --> 01:12:54,470
Just share it.

779
01:12:59,410 --> 01:13:00,470
Mrs. Armstrong?

780
01:13:01,390 --> 01:13:03,190
No, don't get up yet.

781
01:13:03,430 --> 01:13:04,710
Your condition is not yet stable.

782
01:13:04,890 --> 01:13:05,630
Doc, what about my children?

783
01:13:06,290 --> 01:13:07,510
Have they returned to the base?

784
01:13:07,670 --> 01:13:08,210
Not yet.

785
01:13:08,570 --> 01:13:09,990
They're still fighting until now.

786
01:13:12,130 --> 01:13:14,370
Marianne, don't do that, please.

787
01:13:14,610 --> 01:13:15,550
I can do it, Doc.

788
01:13:15,550 --> 01:13:16,890
I can do it on my own.

789
01:13:17,170 --> 01:13:18,330
Please let me go.

790
01:13:18,610 --> 01:13:19,770
You can't do it yet.

791
01:13:19,910 --> 01:13:21,310
You need to rest.

792
01:13:21,510 --> 01:13:23,130
Please, please, please.

793
01:13:24,690 --> 01:13:25,890
Marianne, listen.

794
01:13:26,170 --> 01:13:27,370
No, you listen to me.

795
01:13:28,730 --> 01:13:32,450
I have the authority to leave this medical
bay even if you don't agree with my

796
01:13:32,450 --> 01:13:32,850
decision.

797
01:13:34,150 --> 01:13:35,810
I will leave for my children's sake.

798
01:13:49,330 --> 01:13:54,950
Central Station, concentrate our missiles
to the scout ship to distract them.

799
01:14:09,790 --> 01:14:10,470
Yes, sir.

800
01:14:18,770 --> 01:14:20,210
There's no clear shot of the beast
fighter.

801
01:14:21,170 --> 01:14:22,210
Maybe it was hit by a bolt.

802
01:14:24,330 --> 01:14:25,930
Shall we send a tug to fire, sir?

803
01:14:26,270 --> 01:14:27,290
Then hold on to my command.

804
01:14:30,360 --> 01:14:31,600
It's up to bolt 5 now.

805
01:14:33,860 --> 01:14:34,480
It's up to them.

806
01:14:59,820 --> 01:15:00,620
Ah!

807
01:15:16,320 --> 01:15:19,180
We have to get out of here.

808
01:15:30,910 --> 01:15:34,810
Lieutenant John, divert all power reserves
to thrusters now, please.

809
01:15:35,010 --> 01:15:35,550
Working.

810
01:15:36,890 --> 01:15:39,580
All power reserves to thrusters now.

811
01:16:07,920 --> 01:16:08,520
Sir,

812
01:16:22,160 --> 01:16:24,580
there's an aircraft flying towards the
beast fighter.

813
01:16:26,860 --> 01:16:29,000
I thought you said we don't have pilots.

814
01:16:29,740 --> 01:16:31,180
Then who's flying that?

815
01:16:32,980 --> 01:16:35,720
Chief, contact the pilot now.

816
01:16:39,400 --> 01:16:43,640
On all stars, CBF fighter craft MR5R,
this is Camp Big Falcon Command.

817
01:16:44,360 --> 01:16:45,660
Please identify yourself.

818
01:16:48,060 --> 01:16:51,060
This is Dr. Armstrong flying MR5R over.

819
01:16:57,640 --> 01:16:59,020
I'm so sorry, Richard.

820
01:16:59,800 --> 01:17:01,540
I have to do this for my sons.

821
01:17:02,440 --> 01:17:03,560
I can't let them down.

822
01:17:05,580 --> 01:17:07,680
Marianne, what are you doing?

823
01:17:08,360 --> 01:17:09,260
What's going on, Richard?

824
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:11,240
What's going on, Marianne?

825
01:17:15,590 --> 01:17:18,610
I'm so sorry I can't follow you now,
Richard.

826
01:17:19,430 --> 01:17:22,750
But for all of us here, I have to help
bolt S5.

827
01:17:22,850 --> 01:17:24,130
I have to take care of my children.

828
01:17:24,890 --> 01:17:26,310
So please pray for us.

829
01:17:26,370 --> 01:17:27,030
Come back here.

830
01:17:27,110 --> 01:17:28,270
You'll regret what you're doing.

831
01:17:28,270 --> 01:17:29,450
Too late, Oscar.

832
01:17:30,170 --> 01:17:31,330
I can't let them down.

833
01:17:32,290 --> 01:17:33,910
I can't leave them now.

834
01:17:35,100 --> 01:17:35,710
You're still weak.

835
01:17:36,290 --> 01:17:37,370
You can't do this.

836
01:17:38,750 --> 01:17:41,430
Don't underestimate a mother like me,
Richard.

837
01:17:42,230 --> 01:17:44,110
I can do something to save my children.

838
01:17:47,050 --> 01:17:50,670
So please tell them that I love them so
much.

839
01:17:52,030 --> 01:17:54,330
No matter what happens, don't let them
down.

840
01:17:54,930 --> 01:17:56,870
Please tell them that.

841
01:17:57,810 --> 01:17:58,710
Marianne, no!

842
01:17:59,170 --> 01:17:59,890
That's a negative!

843
01:18:01,750 --> 01:18:03,370
Computer, close transmission.

844
01:18:06,550 --> 01:18:08,590
Sirs, please stop the communication.

845
01:18:09,370 --> 01:18:11,530
Can we try to override the autopilot
system?

846
01:18:11,790 --> 01:18:13,210
It won't override yet.

847
01:18:13,870 --> 01:18:17,210
It has priority alpha access to all CVS
systems.

848
01:18:18,170 --> 01:18:19,070
You can't stop her.

849
01:18:34,430 --> 01:18:35,270
Big Bird!

850
01:18:35,710 --> 01:18:36,250
Little John!

851
01:18:39,090 --> 01:18:39,710
Ah!

852
01:18:40,600 --> 01:18:41,190
Ah!

853
01:18:43,840 --> 01:18:44,430
Ah!

854
01:18:45,650 --> 01:18:46,830
Activate his chain!

855
01:18:47,530 --> 01:18:47,750
Ah!

856
01:18:54,860 --> 01:18:56,040
No!

857
01:18:56,680 --> 01:18:57,620
You can't be Falcon!

858
01:19:11,000 --> 01:19:12,660
Vice Sanger is losing!

859
01:19:12,960 --> 01:19:14,280
Volt is fine!

860
01:19:18,170 --> 01:19:22,650
John Fry, I told you the fight won't last
long.

861
01:19:26,670 --> 01:19:28,450
Look, there's a jet.

862
01:19:28,850 --> 01:19:30,330
They sent help.

863
01:19:30,850 --> 01:19:32,450
I see Little John.

864
01:19:35,660 --> 01:19:41,440
Team, I'm afraid to tell you, but your mom
is flying that fighter jet.

865
01:19:42,000 --> 01:19:42,520
What?

866
01:19:44,560 --> 01:19:45,600
Your mom?

867
01:19:45,960 --> 01:19:48,100
Are you sure your mom is flying that?

868
01:19:59,490 --> 01:20:01,430
Let my sons go!

869
01:20:09,600 --> 01:20:10,400
What's that?

870
01:20:10,920 --> 01:20:11,880
Where did that come from?

871
01:20:34,690 --> 01:20:36,790
your mom is flying that fighter jet.

872
01:20:37,580 --> 01:20:39,110
Why did she allow her to fly?

873
01:20:40,580 --> 01:20:41,890
She ran to the medical bed.

874
01:20:43,110 --> 01:20:47,110
And before we knew it, she commanded one
of the fighter jets.

875
01:20:49,130 --> 01:20:49,770
Mom is so annoying.

876
01:20:50,490 --> 01:20:53,050
Brother, is there a way for us to talk to
her?

877
01:20:53,410 --> 01:20:53,690
Nothing.

878
01:20:54,750 --> 01:20:56,470
Call in through the command center,
Little Jim.

879
01:20:57,630 --> 01:20:58,950
Dr. Smith, please.

880
01:21:00,090 --> 01:21:01,870
Do everything you can to call your mom.

881
01:21:02,830 --> 01:21:04,690
Give her a big falcon, please!

882
01:21:04,970 --> 01:21:07,710
Team, I already did that, but your mom
won't listen.

883
01:21:09,890 --> 01:21:12,870
Dr. Smith, please tell your mom that her
sons are begging here.

884
01:21:13,510 --> 01:21:14,930
Go back to the camp right now!

885
01:21:15,750 --> 01:21:16,650
Tell her that now!

886
01:21:25,280 --> 01:21:29,840
Marianne, because I talked to your sons,
go back to the camp and I agree with them.

887
01:21:30,600 --> 01:21:31,720
Go back to the camp now!

888
01:21:34,140 --> 01:21:35,760
What are you attempting, Marianne?

889
01:21:37,420 --> 01:21:38,700
Marianne, don't do it.

890
01:21:39,320 --> 01:21:39,860
It's suicide.

891
01:22:20,660 --> 01:22:22,560
Computer, open transmission.

892
01:22:28,100 --> 01:22:29,680
My sons, I love you so much.

893
01:22:37,400 --> 01:22:40,380
Mom, don't do this.

894
01:22:42,700 --> 01:22:43,200
Mom!

895
01:22:44,940 --> 01:22:45,720
Mom!

896
01:22:55,730 --> 01:22:56,950
Marianne, abort!

897
01:22:57,630 --> 01:22:58,150
Abort!

898
01:23:03,550 --> 01:23:06,470
Steve, Big Bert, Little John.

899
01:23:08,110 --> 01:23:08,910
Mom!

900
01:23:12,610 --> 01:23:13,830
Mom!

901
01:23:43,650 --> 01:23:44,190
Mom!

902
01:23:49,310 --> 01:23:49,970
Steve!

903
01:24:04,300 --> 01:24:04,740
Mom!

904
01:24:35,680 --> 01:24:36,640
Steve!

905
01:25:05,140 --> 01:25:06,240
That's enough, Little John.

906
01:25:07,900 --> 01:25:09,060
You'll cry later.

907
01:25:11,060 --> 01:25:13,340
Now we need to be stronger.

908
01:25:32,310 --> 01:25:33,010
Mom!

909
01:25:35,590 --> 01:25:36,770
Mom!

910
01:25:37,790 --> 01:25:38,530
Mom!

911
01:25:39,270 --> 01:25:39,750
Mom!

912
01:25:43,340 --> 01:25:43,980
Mom!

913
01:25:56,580 --> 01:25:57,220
Mom!

914
01:25:58,300 --> 01:25:58,700
Mom!

915
01:26:56,430 --> 01:26:57,870
Let's have a match, Mama.

916
01:26:59,010 --> 01:27:01,890
Big Bird, laser sword.

917
01:27:28,790 --> 01:27:30,310
My son, don't let them win.

918
01:27:30,450 --> 01:27:31,690
Wait for their punishment.

919
01:27:52,070 --> 01:27:52,830
Mama!

920
01:28:28,280 --> 01:28:29,040
Mama!

921
01:28:48,980 --> 01:28:50,220
Jules!

922
01:28:50,820 --> 01:28:52,800
Are you saying something?

923
01:28:56,030 --> 01:28:57,770
Natal Montesmay.

924
01:28:59,030 --> 01:29:00,070
Sivay Sanger.

925
01:29:00,810 --> 01:29:01,410
Jennifer...

926
01:29:01,410 --> 01:29:01,710
Wait!

927
01:29:03,270 --> 01:29:05,010
Don't speak!

928
01:29:10,950 --> 01:29:12,190
Jules...

929
01:29:12,190 --> 01:29:14,810
Have we made our new plan?

930
01:29:16,150 --> 01:29:18,390
It's over, Prince Bessartos.

931
01:29:18,390 --> 01:29:20,510
It's over, Prince Bessartos.

932
01:29:20,790 --> 01:29:21,310
It's over.

933
01:30:05,660 --> 01:30:06,360
Mama!

934
01:30:10,940 --> 01:30:12,340
Mama!

935
01:30:41,500 --> 01:30:42,260
I'm sorry.

936
01:30:42,460 --> 01:30:42,980
I feel sorry for the brothers.

937
01:30:44,640 --> 01:30:47,260
It looks like they have lost hope,
sir.

938
01:30:49,400 --> 01:30:50,300
Let's let them cry.

939
01:30:51,540 --> 01:30:52,940
Let them cry like boys.

940
01:30:55,040 --> 01:30:57,820
But I expect that when they stand up
again...

941
01:30:59,720 --> 01:31:02,660
they will rise as warriors...

942
01:31:02,660 --> 01:31:04,760
and avenge their mother and protect our
planet.

943
01:31:18,640 --> 01:31:20,160
Rise, Armstrong brothers.

944
01:31:21,240 --> 01:31:21,920
Rise!

945
01:32:46,280 --> 01:32:50,760
I believe in the warmth of your eyes and
your pain.

946
01:32:53,120 --> 01:32:54,520
Comrades of the Five.

947
01:32:56,080 --> 01:32:58,760
Follow the survivor.

948
01:32:59,780 --> 01:33:02,460
Put everything on the line.

949
01:33:03,500 --> 01:33:08,380
Let's do it, until we run out of strength.

950
01:33:11,640 --> 01:33:13,740
Everyone's smiles...

951
01:33:13,740 --> 01:33:15,840
are magical.

952
01:37:08,760 --> 01:37:11,040
I will not die...

953
01:37:11,620 --> 01:37:14,920
until all the people of Bosnia and
Herzegovina are free.

954
01:37:16,480 --> 01:37:19,420
I am Baron Rothgard.

